1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Mom needs a little space.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Mars Needs Moms is a adventure, animation, family film directed by Simon Wells.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
When Martians suddenly abduct his mom, mischievous Milo rushes to
the rescue and discovers why all moms are so special.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Milo (performance capture), played by Seth Green.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Milo (voice) (as Seth Dusky), played by Seth Robert Dusky.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Mom (voice), played by Joan Cusack.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Gribble (voice), played by Dan Fogler.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Alien (voice), played by Breckin Meyer.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Ki (voice), played by Elisabeth Harnois.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Mars Needs Moms is a 2011 American animated science fiction
comedy film, co-written and directed by Simon Wells.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Based on the Berkeley Breathed book, the film was animated through the process of performance capture
and stars Seth Green, Dan Fogler, Elisabeth Harnois, Mindy Sterling, and Joan Cusack.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It tells the story of a nine-year-old boy named Milo who sets out to
save his mother on Mars after she is abducted by Martians.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Mars Needs Moms premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on March 6, 2011,
and was released in theaters on March 11, 2011 by Walt Disney Pictures.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and was a box-office bomb, grossing $39 million
on a $150 million budget, and losing an estimated $100–144 million for Disney.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film explores themes of rescue, alien, martian,
alien abduction, alien invasion.
